WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.786 --> 00:00:03.350
In 1977, I met a French chef.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.740
He said to me, "Cooks
cook to nurture people."

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.300
That moment is when I decided
to become a professional chef.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.040
It's an emotional
connection that you

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.310
have to have with food,
first and foremost.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.760
This is the first time I've
ever done anything like this.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.950
I've always felt that we
are a product of those

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.210
who have inspired us.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.190
I stand on the shoulders
of countless chefs

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.240
who came before me.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.270
I have better knowledge, I have
better skills because of them.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.740
And that's my job,
to pass it on.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.770
I focus on techniques,
rather than recipes,

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:36.900
because it's really
the techniques that

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.860
are the most important
part of any recipe.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.370
Salt enhances, acid enhances,
pepper changes flavor

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.390
or adds another flavor.

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:50.990
The amount of oil that a yoke
will take is almost infinite.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.140
Glazing is surprisingly
challenging, even

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.330
for professional cooks.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.180
The aromas, the sound
is really important.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.230
Any one of these
techniques is something

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.751
that I know is achievable.

00:01:08.951 --> 00:01:10.700
Every technique that
I'm sharing with you,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.110
we use in our restaurants.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.050
We want to give you
very simple dishes

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.630
with very few ingredients.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.800
It really ignites that
emotional connection to food.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.540
So pan roasting is a technique
to give you creamy, almost

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:24.600
pudding-like zucchini.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.290
If you go through the steps,
if you take your time,

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.230
if you're patient,
you will succeed.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.970
Everything here
that I'm teaching

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:38.670
is something that will
last you a lifetime.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.540
I want you to be able to
master each technique.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.760
You will gain the
confidence and the courage

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:45.580
to express yourself.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.651
I'm Thomas Keller and
this is my MasterClass.

